# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the Python version is usually managed by the user.
#   For a specific project, you might want to keep these files in the repository.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in some cases.
#   However, in others, it is recommended to ignore it.
#   For more information, see:
#   https://pipenv.pypa.io/en/latest/advanced/#pipfile-lock-security-considerations
# Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include poetry.lock in version control.
#   For more information, see:
#   https://python-poetry.org/docs/basic-usage/#commit-your-poetrylock-file-to-version-control
# poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include pdm.lock in version control.
# pdm.lock
#   pdm build working directory
.pdm-build/

# PEP 582; used by e.g. github.com/fannheyward/coc-pyright
